---
import FieldGuideLayout from '../../../components/FieldGuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<FieldGuideLayout
  title="Palette resolution"
  description="Four-tier rule for matching an NCGR to its NCLR: sibling, container-shared, ARM9-pinned external, single-NCLR container."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: '2D Art', href: `${base}/field-guide/2d-art/` },
    { label: 'Palettes' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    NCGR tile data and NCLR palette data are separate
    <a href={`${base}/field-guide/file-formats/nitro-graphics/`}>Nitro</a>
    resources. The right palette for an NCGR is found by walking these rules
    in order; the first match wins.
  </p>

  <h2>BGR555 color format</h2>
  <p>NCLR colors are 16-bit little-endian:</p>
  <pre><code>{`bits 0..4   R  (5 bits)
bits 5..9   G  (5 bits)
bits 10..14 B  (5 bits)
bit 15      ignored on hardware

R8 = (c >> 0)  & 0x1F << 3      # scale 5→8 by left-shifting 3
G8 = (c >> 5)  & 0x1F << 3
B8 = (c >> 10) & 0x1F << 3`}</code></pre>
  <p>Slot 0 is conventionally transparent in OBJ palettes.</p>

  <h2>Palette banks (4bpp NCGR)</h2>
  <p>
    A 4bpp NCGR uses 16-color palettes — but an NCLR can hold many such banks
    (up to 16 banks × 16 colors = 256 entries). The selection of <em>which</em>
    bank applies to a given tile is encoded:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>For BG (NSCR) cells: bits 12..15 of the screen cell word.</li>
    <li>For OBJ (NCER) cells: bits 12..15 of OAM <code>attr2</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When an NCLR has 2+ sections, the <code>PMCP</code> section maps each
    local bank index to a VRAM bank index. Without <code>PMCP</code>, banks
    are assumed sequential <code>0..N-1</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Four-tier resolution rule</h2>

  <h3>Tier 1: Sibling NCLR in same RESO</h3>
  <p>
    Within a container, the NCLR adjacent to the NCGR (in TOC index order,
    immediately following the NCGR or preceding the next NCGR sentinel) is
    the sibling palette. Implemented by <code>group_siblings()</code> in
    <code>src/translator/_sprite_assoc.py</code>. Covers the
    NCGR/NCLR/NCER triplet pattern.
  </p>

  <h3>Tier 2: Container-wide shared NCLR</h3>
  <p>
    When a container batches several NCGRs at the start with no per-NCGR
    NCLR, the container's first NCLR serves all of them. Used by
    <code>buyitem.lzs</code> and similar shop containers (5 NCGRs + 3 shared
    NCLRs + 6 NSCRs).
  </p>

  <h3>Tier 3: ARM9-pinned external NCLR</h3>
  <p>
    The palette lives in a different container, pinned by ARM9 loader code.
    Empirically resolved mappings:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Source container (NCGRs)</th><th>NCGR count</th><th>bpp</th><th>Palette container + entry</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>item/itemicon.ofs</code></td><td>656</td><td>8bpp</td>
        <td><code>global.lzs</code> RESO entry 5</td>
        <td>256-color. Entry 6 = grayed-out variant.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>2d/inputmagic/mgcall.ofs</code></td><td>389</td><td>4bpp</td>
        <td><code>2d/inputmagic/mgc80.ofs</code> entry 0</td>
        <td>16-color. Entry 2 = alt scheme.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>2d/inputmagic/mgc01..09c.lzs</code></td><td>823 total</td><td>4bpp</td>
        <td><code>2d/inputmagic/mgc80.ofs</code> entry 0</td>
        <td>Shared with mgcall.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Tier 4: Single-NCLR container</h3>
  <p>
    When a container has exactly one NCLR (e.g.
    <code>trendranking/npcicon.ofs</code> — 141 NCGRs + 1 NCLR), that single
    NCLR is the shared palette for every NCGR. The sibling heuristic alone
    misses this because the NCLR isn't grouped adjacent.
  </p>

  <h3>Fallback</h3>
  <p>Render with a grayscale palette. Used as a last resort.</p>

  <h2>Resolution stats</h2>
  <p>
    From <code>notes/palette_association.json</code> (4,337 total NCGR groups):
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Render kind</th><th>Count</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>NSCR BG screen</td><td>1,099</td></tr>
      <tr><td>NCER cell composition</td><td>926</td></tr>
      <tr><td>External magic glyph</td><td>823</td></tr>
      <tr><td>External item icon</td><td>656</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Single sprite</td><td>466</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tilebank-only</td><td>296</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Orphan (no palette resolved)</td><td>469</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Of the remaining 469 orphan NCGRs, the bulk are in:
    <code>2d/signboard.lzs</code> (80), <code>2d/designlogo.lzs</code> (74),
    <code>2d/designcloth.lzs</code> (58), <code>2d/selmaterial.lzs</code> (52),
    <code>2d/expect.ofs</code> (51), <code>2d/buyitem.lzs</code> (31, shop bg
    variants).
  </p>

  <h2>ARM9 external-palette evidence (item icons)</h2>
  <p>
    The 256-color OBJ palette for <code>item/itemicon.ofs</code> lives in
    <code>global.lzs</code>, RESO entries 5 (main) and 6 (greyed-out). Each
    NCLR is a 570-byte chunk with <code>bpp_code=4</code> (8bpp = 256
    colors), <code>palette_data_size=512</code>. The loader is the generic
    asset-loader at <code>0x02052D20</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`02052D4C  LDR  R0, [PC, #0x30]      ; r0 = 0x020AA740  (item-list ptr)
02052D4E  LDR  R1, [PC, #0x34]      ; r1 = 0x020A55D8  ("item/itemicon.ofs")
02052D50  LSLS R3, R3, #0xA          ; r3 = 0x7800     (flags)
02052D52  BLX  0x02009894            ; call generic file-loader
                                     ; r2 = u16 sub-index from caller's [r5+0x84]
`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    No static <code>(icon_index → palette_index)</code> table exists because
    none is needed: every item icon uses the same global OBJ palette uploaded
    once at boot from <code>global.lzs</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Discovering external mappings</h2>
  <p>Recipe used when palette mapping is unknown:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Determine NCGR bpp distribution in the container.</li>
    <li>If 4bpp → palette is 16-color (32 bytes + header). If 8bpp → 256-color (512 bytes + header).</li>
    <li>Histogram palette indices used across all NCGRs in the container. Clustering in one half of the index range constrains which slots must be populated.</li>
    <li>Filter candidate NCLRs by color count and visual content (slot 0 is often a saturated transparency key).</li>
    <li>Score each candidate by color variety of actually-used indices when rendered.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>src/translator/_sprite_assoc.py</code> — sibling + container scanner</li>
    <li><code>src/translator/_build_assoc_v2.py</code> — produces <code>palette_association.json</code></li>
    <li><code>notes/palette_association.json</code> — full mapping</li>
    <li><code>notes/asset_extraction_methodology.md</code> §"Palette association hierarchy"</li>
  </ul>
</FieldGuideLayout>
